We thus aimed to extract a design for the most optimized peptide variant using significant pattern mining [30]. This method looks for significantly enriched combinations of three amino acid residues among the 10% and 25% (arbitrary threshold set by us; Table 1; full dataset in Additional file 7) most and least antimicrobial peptides. A specific combination of four amino acid residues cannot be enriched in a fraction, as it appears only in a single peptide. In addition, as also previously stated, single data points in an NGS-based ranking can be error-prone. We thus investigated enrichment among all triple amino acid residue combinations (in total 32,000 = \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
